    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "Release store: earlier writes are visible first. Acquire load: later reads happen after it.",
      "narration": "A release store makes all earlier writes visible before it. An acquire load ensures later reads happen after it. Pair them on the same variable.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Acquire and release in C11",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 8,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "c",
          "text": "data = 42;\nstore_explicit(&flag, 1,\n  memory_order_release);\n\nwhile (!load_explicit(&flag,\n  memory_order_acquire));\nuse(data);",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 33.8,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "caption": "If the acquire reads the release's value, the writer's earlier stores happen-before the reader's later loads.",
      "narration": "When the acquire load reads the value the release stored, the two synchronize. Everything before the release now happens-before everything after the acquire.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Synchronizes-with",
